ParentVault_ccipReceive
├── when caller is not the CCIPRouter
│   └── it should revert with InvalidRouter
├── when sender is not the allowed sender for the source chain
│   └── it should revert with BaseVault__InvalidSender
├── when received token is not USDC
│   └── it should revert with BaseVault__InvalidReceivedToken
├── when token amounts length is zero
│   └── it should revert with BaseVault__InvalidTokenAmountsLength
├── when token amounts length is greater than one
│   └── it should revert with BaseVault__InvalidTokenAmountsLength
├── when received amount is zero
│   └── it should revert with BaseVault__NoZeroAmount
├── when tx type is invalid
│   └── it should revert with BaseVault__InvalidTxType
├── when message is a withdraw
│   ├── when the decoded epoch nonce does not match the previous epoch nonce
│   │   └── it should revert with ParentVault__InvalidEpochNonce
│   ├── when the epoch is not executing
│   │   └── it should revert with ParentVault__EpochNotExecuting
│   ├── when the received USDC amount is less than the epoch withdraw obligation
│   │   ├── it should make the epoch claimable
│   │   ├── it should emit EpochWithdrawAmountShort
│   │   └── it should update the withdraw claim amount and remaining withdraw claim amount
│   ├── when the received USDC amount matches the epoch withdraw obligation
│   │   ├── it should make the epoch claimable
│   │   ├── it should update the withdraw claim amount and remaining withdraw claim amount
│   │   └── it should emit EpochClaimable
│   └── when the received USDC amount is greater than the epoch withdraw obligation
│       ├── it should make the epoch claimable
│       ├── it should update the withdraw claim amount and remaining withdraw claim amount
│       └── it should emit EpochClaimable
└── when message is a rebalance
    ├── when there is no rebalance in progress
    │   └── it should revert with ParentVault__NoRebalanceInProgress
    ├── when the decoded rebalance nonce does not match
    │   └── it should revert with ParentVault__InvalidRebalanceNonce
    ├── when the decoded protocol id does not match the pending protocol id
    │   └── it should revert with ParentVault__InvalidPendingProtocolId
    ├── when the target protocol adapter is not registered
    │   └── it should revert with BaseVault__NoAdapterRegistered
    ├── when the target adapter deposit succeeds
    │   ├── it should deposit bridged USDC into the target adapter
    │   ├── it should set the active protocol adapter
    │   ├── it should finalize the rebalance
    │   ├── it should emit RebalanceDepositSuccess
    │   └── it should emit RebalanceCompleted
    └── when the target adapter deposit reverts
        ├── it should emit RebalanceDepositFailure
        ├── it should store rebalance deposit recovery
        ├── it should emit RebalanceDepositRecoveryStored
        ├── it should leave the rebalance in progress
        └── when rebalance deposit recovery already exists
            └── it should revert with BaseVault__RecoveryAlreadyPending
